&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 72pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;(1) Assets recoverable without earning a return.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Our significant regulatory assets and liabilities include:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-style: italic;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-style: italic;"&gt;Taxes on capitalized funds used during construction.&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Amounts represent the deferred income taxes on AFUDC equity funds. These amounts are recoverable in our tariff rates over the depreciable lives of the assets to which they apply.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-style: italic;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-style: italic;"&gt;Income tax related.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-style: italic;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Amounts represent the anticipated return to ratepayers of deferred income taxes as a result of the Tax Cuts and Jobs Act of 2017, which lowered the U.S. federal corporate income tax rate from 35% to 21% effective January 1, 2018. These amounts are amortized to Account 411.1 &amp;#8220;Provision for Deferred Income Taxes &amp;#8211; Credit&amp;#8221; over the remaining depreciable lives of the assets to which they apply.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-style: italic;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-style: italic;"&gt;Difference between gas retained and gas consumed in operations. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Amounts reflect the value of the difference between the quantity of gas retained for fuel and the quantity of gas consumed in our operations. Pursuant to our tariff, the quantities associated with these amounts are expected to be recovered from or returned to our customers in subsequent periods. On a periodic basis, we file reports with the FERC detailing our volumetric fuel activity and establishing prospective fuel retention rates. Volumetric over- or under-collections of fuel quantities from prior periods are trued up through either an addition or reduction to the prospective fuel retention rates.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;For the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, we recorded net regulatory expenses of $102 thousand and $186 thousand, respectively, related to our fuel activity.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;7. Recent Accounting Pronouncement&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;ASU No. 2025-06&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;On September 18, 2025, the Financial Accounting Standards Board issued ASU No. 2025-06, &amp;#8220;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-style: italic;"&gt;Intangibles&amp;#8212;Goodwill and Other&amp;#8212;Internal-Use Software (Subtopic 350-40): Targeted Improvements to the Accounting for Internal-Use Software.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#8221; This ASU modernizes the accounting guidance for the costs to develop software for internal use by removing outdated stage-based cost capitalization rules and replacing them with a probability-based cost-capitalization framework that aligns better with current software development methods. This ASU will be effective for annual periods beginning after December 15, 2027, for interim reporting periods beginning within those annual periods, and early adoption is permitted. Management is currently evaluating this ASU to determine its impact on the Company's financial statements.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
